#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:9
msgid "Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:11
msgid "Run `hero scan --code` first to ensure the code index is current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Call `hero_code` with `action: unenriched` to get a batch of symbols "
"needing descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:13
msgid ""
"For each symbol, read the source context and write a concise one-line "
"description of what it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:14
msgid "Call `hero_enrich` with the descriptions as a JSON array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:15
msgid "Repeat steps 2-4 until no more unenriched symbols are returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:17
msgid "Description Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"One sentence, starts with a verb (e.g. \"Handles incoming MCP tool calls "
"and dispatches to handlers\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:20
msgid "Focus on what the symbol DOES, not its signature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Be specific to the codebase, not generic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:22
msgid "For types/structs: describe what they represent and their role"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:23
msgid "For functions: describe the primary behavior and key side effects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/deep-code-enrichment/SKILL.md:24
msgid "Skip trivial getters/setters — describe the business purpose instead"
msgstr ""

